    "id": "p16-q51-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "51",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following algebraic fractions.\n$$\\frac{\\dfrac2{x^2-y^2}}{\\dfrac1{x+y}+\\dfrac1{x-y}}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac1x$, for real $x,y$ with $x\\ne0$ and $x\\ne\\pm y$.",
      "worked": "Multiply top and bottom by $x^2-y^2=(x-y)(x+y)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\frac2{x^2-y^2}}{\\frac1{x+y}+\\frac1{x-y}}&=\\frac2{(x-y)+(x+y)}\\\\\\frac{\\frac2{x^2-y^2}}{\\frac1{x+y}+\\frac1{x-y}}&=\\frac2{2x}\\\\\\frac{\\frac2{x^2-y^2}}{\\frac1{x+y}+\\frac1{x-y}}&=\\frac1x\\end{align*}$$\nOriginal domain: real $x,y$ with $x\\ne0$ and $x\\ne\\pm y$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 32
  },
